	"metadata": {
		"app_version": "0.1.0",
		"created": "2026-10-18T12:00:00",
		"description": "Firmware example: the two firmware-driven actuators on one board - an SG90 servo on D9 (through the virtual pin P1) and an A4988 STEP/DIR driver on D3/D2 (through P2/P3) turning a NEMA 17. The sketch firmware/sketches/motion_demo drives both at once.",
		"measurement": "Compile firmware/sketches/motion_demo for arduino:avr:uno, then run_firmware(hex_path, ms=1500, pin_map={\"9\": \"P1\", \"3\": \"P2\", \"2\": \"P3\"}). The response reports the servo under `servos` (angle_deg 90.7 after the 0..180 sweep settles at 90) and the stepper under `steppers` (steps 150 = +200 forward then -50 reverse, angle_deg 270). apply_firmware_servo / apply_firmware_stepper write those onto S1.angle and M1.steps/M1.angle. Both are mechanical, so the solved circuit does not change; only the actuators are modelled (the driver's straps and current limit are not).",
		"modified": "2026-10-18T12:00:00",
		"name": "Firmware Motion (Servo + STEP/DIR Stepper)"
	},
